// CotSC localisation - bg0200_baldurs_gate.d
// English translation reference. Translate the text after each @number.

@1 = ~Move along, citizen.~
@2 = ~Not that I want to make wrong assumptions but you look as if you haven't taken a bath in a long while.~
@3 = ~I don't like the look of you. You probably could say the same thing about me but my point remains.~
@4 = ~And yet the world keeps going, paladin.~
@5 = ~Unbelievable that Flaming Fist allows these filthy mongrels in the city. Baldur's Gate reputation for tolerance never escaped my notice but I was hoping for a tiny bit more lawfulness in its rules.~
@6 = ~May Yondalla always shine the path you walk on, stranger.~
@7 = ~Want to crunch on elf meat so bad... but Fist guards watch close. Miss the wilds. In the trees, I hunt elves, eat well, no rules. Now? Naught to chew but dry bread. Makes me sick.~
@8 = ~What?~
@9 = ~Fat... belly? I don't want fat belly. You keep away, I do not want to see elves anymore.~
@10 = ~Hold your horses, my Orcish brute friend. Your interest in my appetizing body and palatable insides is comprehensible, albeit inaccurate. Our meat is a little chewy and stringy. I'm sure your culinary practices are commendable and incomparable but do you know what can happen to you long-term if you eat elven meat?~
@11 = ~Elven meat causes excessive increases in body fat due to the rich, otherworldly nectar of our diet. An orc's stomach cannot process it, turning it instantly into round, soft fat—specifically around the chest and hips. You won't look like a terrifying warrior of the wilds anymore; you'll look like a plump, well-fed tavern keeper. Your pals will laugh you out all the way, my friend.~
@12 = ~Brutish, just like the vast number of these creatures are. Elves have no love for orcs, and for a good historical reason.~
@13 = ~Certainly, of all ways I could end my miserable existence, being roasted by a hungry ugliness such as this is low down the list. Very low.~
@14 = ~Leave me alone.~
@15 = ~Me thank you for advice you gave me.~
@16 = ~What do you want?~
@17 = ~Why are you hiding here?~
@18 = ~Nothing~
@19 = ~People not like me. Me be new in city. Me not like it. Feel weird.~
@20 = ~Did you try try talking to some other hobgoblins around?~
@21 = ~I can't help you.~
@22 = ~No. Me get a house. Owner is half-elf. She be nice but not one else be nice. Me no job. Mistake to come here.~
@23 = ~The hardest part is behind you. You moved in. In a big city full of strangers where your species feel out of place. But other hobgoblins accommodated so if they could, you definitely can.~
@24 = ~You're a hobgoblin after all. Your kind is murderous.~
@25 = ~I can't help you.~
@26 = ~You... are right. Me give up easy. Me want to be friends with others. Thank you, <PRO_RACE>. Me try harder now.~
@27 = ~Me not like your opinion. Priest of Helm bless me and tell me I not a bad person. You mean. Don't talk to me anymore.~
@28 = ~What you said to that poor lad was out of place, <CHARNAME>. Not nice!~
@29 = ~Do you know Mystra? Mommy taught me she is a goddess of magic. I want to learn magic, like my daddy did. Mommy says I shouldn't because daddy wasn't careful. He opened a portal to go to work one day and he never came back. Mommy says he is far away now, and sometimes she cries. I think it's because she misses him. But I'll be careful when learning and one day I shall make my mom proud. I'll open a portal and take my mom to dad. I miss him.~
@30 = ~Walk away. I don't want people to see me with a vagabond.~
@31 = ~Come on! Come all! Hot drinks! Cold drinks! Meals! All at a decent price!~
@32 = ~Tell me about it. Inciting people to come to the tavern isn't as simple as it seems. The owners are really good to me, however, and pay for hot meals and drinks if I ever need any.~
@33 = ~Come and find out. Historically, the Three Old Kegs is widely regarded as one of the best, cosiest and most tolerant inns in the region, famous for its comfortable furnishings and relaxed atmosphere. Best chicken, solid beer, and sometimes you can even enjoy entertainment from clowns who get drunk, start arguing with one another and spill their wildest secrets in public. Fun!~
@34 = ~We aren't doing anything suspicious here. Hehe. Not at all...~
@35 = ~Shh, brother. Someone is coming... Hey there. Nice day, huh? Heh.~
@36 = ~You must be spending plenty of time out here, straining your voice, screaming at the top of your lungs.~
@37 = ~Is this place any good?~
@38 = ~Chicken. You serve products of nature as meals in a crowded city. It's unnatural. Keeping chickens in cramped cages within human cities, breeding livestock on an industrial scale or killing them for gluttonous human waste... Had I a bigger say, things would change.~
